From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 05:39:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add node_has_pending_image for srcset-mutation complete
 tracking

A src/srcset mutation re-runs load_image, which either applies a
cached image synchronously (no delivery notification) or starts a
fetch (delivery notification later). The kitesurf dom-shim marks the
<img> pending-reload on every mutation, but for the synchronous
cache-hit path no notification ever clears the flag, so
HTMLImageElement.complete sticks false forever. That breaks React
components polling img.complete post-hydration (BBC's Image
placeholder never unmounts and paints over the real image).

node_has_pending_image lets the JS side ask, right after the
mutation, whether a fetch is actually underway for the node. The
shim can't answer this itself: srcset candidate selection lives in
the mutator (select_image_url) and the shim doesn't know which URL
blitz picked.
---
 src/document.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/document.rs b/src/document.rs
index 0c70114..06dd1f9 100644
--- a/src/document.rs
+++ b/src/document.rs
@@ -1629,5 +1629,21 @@ impl BaseDocument {
             .unwrap_or_default()
     }

+    /// Whether `node_id` is currently waiting on an
+    /// in-flight image fetch (any URL). Complements image_cache_has
+    /// for the srcset case: the JS side can't re-run candidate
+    /// selection, so after a src/srcset mutation it asks whether
+    /// load_image actually started a fetch. Not pending = the
+    /// mutation reached a terminal state synchronously (cache-hit
+    /// apply, or no fetchable candidate) and no delivery
+    /// notification will ever fire.
+    pub fn node_has_pending_image(&self, node_id: NodeId) -> bool {
+        self.pending_images.values().any(|waiting| {
+            waiting
+                .iter()
+                .any(|(id, ty)| *id == node_id && matches!(ty, ImageType::Image))
+        })
+    }
+
     pub fn load_resource(&mut self, res: ResourceLoadResponse) {
         self.pending_critical_resources.remove(&res.request_id);
